From 65aa5a6d4cc047559b9e633b91534ee5fa920310 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:58:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: remove the dead mana-cost test from the Venom
 preparation

borg_perma_aux_venom() was copied from the Smite Evil routine and still
read the cost of SMITE_EVIL.  Only the Blackguard has Venom and the
Blackguard has no Smite Evil, so the cost came back as -1.  The test
"cost >= current spell points / 10 (or / 7)" could then only refuse the
cast with negative spell points, while borg_spell_okay_fail(VENOM) just
above already requires the spell points to cover Venom's cost of 18.
The test always passed.

Remove the cost lookup and the test, keeping the current behaviour: the
Blackguard prepares Venom without a mana-cost limit.  No behaviour
change.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#111.
---
 src/borg/borg-fight-perm.c | 10 +---------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-fight-perm.c b/src/borg/borg-fight-perm.c
index aff0e0ffd..c957b5042 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-fight-perm.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-fight-perm.c
@@ -521,7 +521,7 @@ static int borg_perma_aux_smite_evil(void)
  */
 static int borg_perma_aux_venom(void)
 {
-    int fail_allowed = 5, cost;
+    int fail_allowed = 5;
 
     /* increase the threshold */
     if (borg.mon.unique)
@@ -540,14 +540,6 @@ static int borg_perma_aux_venom(void)
     if (!borg_spell_okay_fail(VENOM, fail_allowed))
         return 0;
 
-    /* Obtain the cost of the spell */
-    cost = borg_get_spell_power(SMITE_EVIL);
-
-    /* If its cheap, go ahead */
-    if (cost >= ((borg.mon.unique) ? borg.trait[BI_CURSP] / 7
-                                   : borg.trait[BI_CURSP] / 10))
-        return 0;
-
     /* Simulation */
     /* smite evil is a low priority */
     if (borg_simulate)
-- 
